course: dictionary
lesson: 7724
title: Words with a homeland
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words travel from one language to another, and they bring their meaning with them. «Pueblo» comes from Spanish, where it means town, village or people. Use the clues around the word to work out which meaning fits.
explain: «In the dry Southwest the Ancestral Puebloans built houses of stone and adobe in cliffs and canyons.» A dry, desert place and houses of stone and adobe tell you a pueblo is a village of buildings. Adobe is mud brick, so the houses are made from materials the land provides.
explain: Capital letters give a clue. «Pueblo peoples still live there today» has a capital P because it names groups of people, such as the Hopi, Zuni and Taos. A small p, as in «a pueblo», means one village. Ask yourself: is the sentence naming people, or a building?
explain: Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it. «The Pueblo peoples of the desert were just as different» still makes sense if you read it as "the Native American nations of the desert", so the capital P means people.
fact: A pueblo is a village of flat-roofed houses made of adobe (mud brick) or stone.
fact: Pueblo peoples are Native American nations, such as the Hopi, Zuni and Taos, who live in these villages.
fact: «Pueblo» came into English from Spanish, where it means town, village or people.
fact: Taos Pueblo in New Mexico has been lived in for about 1,000 years.
fact: Pueblo houses have thick walls that keep them cool in the desert.
exercise: «In the dry Southwest the Ancestral Puebloans built houses of stone and adobe.» What is a pueblo? | A cold house made of ice | *A village of flat-roofed houses made of adobe or stone | A desert full of cactus and sand | A type of Spanish dance
exercise: «The Pueblo peoples of the desert were just as different.» What does the capital P in Pueblo tell you? | It means a kind of mud brick | It names a river in New Mexico | *It names Native American nations | It is the start of a new sentence only
exercise: Where did the word pueblo come from? | Greek | *Spanish | Lakota | Inuit
test: Why are pueblo houses cool in the desert? | Their roofs are made of ice | *Their thick walls keep them cool | They are built under water | They are painted bright white
test: How long has Taos Pueblo been lived in? | Since last week | *About 1,000 years | About 100 years | Ten years
exam: What does the small p word mean in «a pueblo of flat-roofed houses»? | *A village | A king | A river | A dance
